.TH SAPHIRA-IMAGE-CREATOR-MENU 8 "October 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
saphira-image-creator-menu \- console menu for the USB image-creator appliance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-image-creator-menu
.SH DESCRIPTION
The creator appliance boots into this menu instead of a login
prompt. Its sole purpose is writing Saphira/SaphiraD destination systems
to real disks (BIOS or UEFI; ext4 or ZFS root).
.PP
This menu never sets destination credentials, networking, or DNS. It
writes a locked-root destination; ordinary
.BR saphira-firstboot (8)
owns the root password, user creation, networking, and DNS on the
destination's first boot. Destination disks are chosen by stable
.I /dev/disk/by-id/
identifiers; mounted disks are refused.
.PP
The menu offers exactly four destination products:
.BR "BIOS Saphira" ,
.BR "UEFI Saphira" ,
.BR "BIOS SaphiraD" ,
and
.BR "UEFI SaphiraD" .
The engine's internal build-target matrix is not shown here; installer
media and minimal rescue/test targets cannot be selected for a disk
write.
.PP
This is a network-dependent creator: writing is refused unless
.I packages.saphira.vm2.uk
answers ping (IPv4 then IPv6, 3-second reply timeout each). Use
.B Setup network
(DHCP or static IPv4/IPv6 with DNS) first; a failed check returns to
the main menu without touching any disk.
.PP
If the menu process fails repeatedly, systemd starts the local
.B saphira-image-creator-recovery.service
console on the same tty instead of leaving a dead screen. The recovery
console is a local root shell; it does not enable SSH and does not set
destination credentials. The ordinary installer menu stays masked on
this appliance.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_REPOSITORY
Package repository used for destination installs (default:
.IR https://packages.saphira.vm2.uk/hatched ).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_CREATOR_DISK
Skip device enumeration and use this path (test/operator override).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_CREATOR_DIALOG
Menu backend (default: dialog).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_CREATOR_TTY
Console device (default: /dev/tty1, falling back to /dev/console).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira-image (8),
.BR saphira-install-menu (8),
.BR saphira-firstboot (8)
